LOGO DESIGN BRIEF - MARKETING MAIN STREET

So here's the deal. We've been running Marketing Main Street since 2021 out of Stuart, Iowa. Nate (that's me, the founder) previously owned Ruby's Pub for about a decade before pivoting into digital marketing. We help small businesses across Central Iowa get seen online - that's pretty much our whole thing.

Currently serving about 18 cities: Des Moines, Waukee, West Des Moines, Ankeny, Clive, Urbandale, Perry, and a bunch more surrounding areas. Web design, video production, social media, SEO - the usual marketing stuff for local businesses.

What we need:

A new logo. The current one isn't bad or anything, it's just... it's had its run, you know? Feels a little dated and honestly it doesn't really capture what we're about anymore. Looking for something that speaks to Iowa small business owners without looking like every other generic marketing agency out there.

Design direction-wise: Midwest vibes but keep it modern. We're talking restaurants, contractors, salons, bakeries - all kinds of local businesses. Should feel approachable, trustworthy. Not flashy, not corporate. Small-town friendly but professionally done.

Colors: we've been using orange/coral as the main accent with blue as secondary. Doesn't have to stay exactly the same but should keep some connection. Just make sure it works for both digital stuff and print.

Typography: clean and readable first. Needs to look good small (like favicon size) and large (website header). Sans-serif probably makes more sense for our industry, but honestly if something with more character fits the Iowa vibe, we're open to it.

Deliverables we need:

1. Primary logo in full color
2. Black/white version
3. Reversed version for dark backgrounds
4. Icon-only version for social media profiles
5. All vector files (AI, EPS, SVG)
6. PNG exports at 300dpi in 512x512, 1024x1024, 2000x2000

Technical stuff:

File formats: AI, EPS, SVG, PDF, PNG
Resolution: minimum 300dpi for raster formats
Safe zone: 10% padding around elements
Color mode: CMYK for print, RGB for digital

Process: we'll want to see 3 initial concepts before deciding on direction. Then up to 2 rounds of revisions on the chosen one.

Contact me at nate@marketingmainstreet.co if you're interested. Send along examples of similar work you've done - marketing agencies or local businesses preferred.


INITIAL DRAFT - LOGO IDEAS (Internal Notes)

Quick notes from our team discussion on the logo redesign:

- Current logo's been working okay for the past few years but honestly it's getting a bit stale
- Want to stand out from the typical Iowa marketing agency look
- Orange/coral is our thing - not abandoning it completely
- Primary use cases: website header, social icons, business cards, proposals
- Nate wants something that feels more like us but nothing crazy wild

Brands we're inspired by:
- Local coffee shop aesthetics (cozy, welcoming vibes)
- Modern farm-to-table restaurant branding
- Clean fintech startups but less sterile

What we're NOT going for:
- Big corporate feel
- Too cutesy or playful
- Fonts that look cheap

Nick (handles our web stuff) mentioned we should probably have a version that works as an app icon too. Good call honestly.


BRAND REFERENCES AND MOOD BOARD

Visual direction we're aiming for:

1. Warm colors - like that golden hour light over Iowa fields in the evening
2. Typography that's clean but has some character
3. Geometric shapes that feel solid but friendly
4. Maybe some subtle nods to Iowa geography/architecture without being literal

Competitor landscape:

Most Iowa marketing agencies fall into one of two buckets:
a) Corporate blue/gray look - too impersonal for what we're doing
b) Overly rustic/barnwood aesthetic - doesn't really fit our tech-forward side

We're trying to land somewhere in between. Local agency feel but with modern chops.

Our clients shape the direction too:
- Construction companies and contractors
- Restaurants and cafes
- Beauty salons and spas
- Fitness studios
- Local retail shops

These are business owners who probably don't think of themselves as super creative people but want something that makes them look legit and trustworthy.

Current site colors: Orange (#F97316) and dark blue (#1E3A8A).


TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS AND DELIVERY SPECS

Files we need:

Vector formats (must have):
- Adobe Illustrator (.ai)
- EPS (.eps) - older software compatibility
- SVG (.svg)
- PDF

Raster formats:
- PNG at 300dpi: 512x512, 1024x1024, 2000x2000, plus original proportions
- JPEG at 300dpi: 1024x1024, 2000x2000
- Web PNGs: 100x100, 200x200, 400x400

Color versions needed:
- Full color primary
- Black version
- White/reversed for dark backgrounds
- Grayscale

Social media stuff:
- Square icon 1:1 at 500x500px minimum
- Profile pic: 400x400px
- Favicon: 16x16, 32x32, 48x48px

Print sizing to keep in mind:
- Business cards: readable at 1 inch wide
- Vehicle wrap: scales up to 6 feet
- Letterhead: readable at 2 inches

Font stuff:
- Keep text layers editable where possible
- Outlines for non-editable versions
- Tell us what fonts were used

Brand guidelines doc should include:
- All color codes (HEX, RGB, CMYK, Pantone)
- Clear space minimums
- Do's and don'ts for using the logo
- Font pairing ideas

By main

